## MOF Catalysts
Presence versus Proximity: The Role of Pendant Amines in the Catalytic Hydrolysis of a Nerve Agent Simulant
Proximity De-pendant: The role of amino groups on the hydrolysis of a nerve agent simulant, DMNP, has been explored. Experiments and theoretical calculations reveal that not only the presence but also the proximity of the amino group is important for effective chemical detoxification of DMNP. NU-1002-o-\(\mathsf{N H}_{2}\), a Zr-based mesoporous metal–organic framework (MOF) with pendant amines demonstrates\(^{t_{1/2}}\) of 1.2 min with only 3 mol% catalyst loading.
